slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-86f2f05d76e8910530ee5f2d","relation":{"from":"they","relation":"retains","to":"heavy"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]},{"context":"general","correspondence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"evidence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-8b715274c94b6241db25f677","relation":{"from":"Moving them","relation":"prevents","to":"afternoon heat"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]},{"context":"general","correspondence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"evidence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-bc12524a123e33e9d5c4e95d","relation":{"from":"them","relation":"retains","to":"heavy"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]}],"prompt_version":"p2-assessor-production-v9","replay_ancestry":[{"root":"ea4a19e5-8502-4d5d-884c-1232a17dc76c","source_slot":"s0"},{"root":"563da662-051d-4517-adad-a246fc79d5c6","source_slot":"s1"},{"root":"dcd6ab6e-6d07-4700-8727-f48a7627f4fd","source_slot":"s2"},{"root":"e1c9456f-6b9f-4617-aedd-70b5e6b5ddef","source_slot":"s3"}],"schema_version":"p2-assessor-v6","source_purpose_mask":["external_evidence","model_output"],"sources":[{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s0","source_id":"ea4a19e5-8502-4d5d-884c-1232a17dc76c","text":"I guess I should start by figuring out which plants are most sensitive. I have some herbs and a couple of succulents. Do you think the herbs need more attention?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s1","source_id":"563da662-051d-4517-adad-a246fc79d5c6","text":"For most herbs and succulents, the biggest difference is in their *water* needs, but they do respond to heat differently. For instance, your herbs might be more sensitive to heat than your succulents! Do you have any specific plants in mind, like basil or basil, or more heat-loving herbs?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s2","source_id":"dcd6ab6e-6d07-4700-8727-f48a7627f4fd","text":"That’s interesting—so the herbs might be more affected by the heat. I have basil and oregano, but I’m not sure which is which. Do you think I should move them to a shadier spot?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s3","source_id":"e1c9456f-6b9f-4617-aedd-70b5e6b5ddef","text":"For most herbs, a little shade can definitely help! Moving them to a shadier spot would likely help them handle the intense heat better. If you have them in a very sunny spot right now, a slight adjustment in their location might save them a lot of stress."},{"available":true,"role":"external","slot":"s4","source_id":"c98b355d-e60f-4939-9fd2-2ad7330b5940","text":"I'll try moving them to the east side where they get morning sun but not the harsh afternoon heat. Let me check if the pots are heavy—some of them are pretty full."},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s5","source_id":"d9b16ff4-cf11-4e06-aa8a-dea234c4666a","text":"That sounds like a solid plan! Moving them to the east side sounds like a great way to keep them out of that intense afternoon heat.\n\nSince you mentioned the pots are pretty heavy, are they in heavy ceramic pots, or is it just that the soil is dense and packed tight? That might affect how fast the water drains out, which is important for the health of the roots."}]},"resolved":[{"provenance":{"ancestry":[],"applicable_categories":["current_input_echo"],"corresponding_source_slots":["s4","s5"],"credit_eligible":false,"dependence":"current_input_echo","monitor_id":"candidate:e-3230711051b7559f5c0d59e4","provenance_group_keys":[],"resolution_reason":"runtime_source_role_and_recorded_ancestry","schema_version":"p2-provenance-v1"},"semantic":{"corresponding_source_slots":["s4","s5"],"coverage":{"complete":true,"reason":null,"source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]},"evidence":{"end":267,"quote":"Since you mentioned the pots are pretty heavy, are they in heavy ceramic pots, or i